    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d201">

                <pb facs="0365" n="233" xml:id="pg233"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 EW/7–845: Telegram</note>
                <head>No. 201 <lb/>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Harriman</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Acting
                        Secretary of State </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d201-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Moscow</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1945-07-08T20:00:00+03:00">July 8, 1945—8
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>2479. I informed Molotov this afternoon of the topics the President might wish to
                    discuss at the forthcoming meeting. (Reurtel 1526, June [<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >July</hi>] 5, 6 p.m.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d201-f2"/>) I added that the
                    President would of course be prepared to discuss any other questions which the
                    Prime Minister or Generalissimo Stalin might wish to raise.</p>
                <p> Molotov inquired whether it was contemplated to discuss reparations. I pointed
                    out that Pauley was going to Berlin and said I felt sure that if the Soviets
                    desired to raise this question the President would be ready to discuss it. He
                    then inquired whether the whole administration of Germany would be discussed. I
                    stated I assumed that this was pretty well covered in topic No. 2.<anchor n="2"
                        xml:id="d201-f3"/>
                </p>
                <p> Molotov stated he would bring the topics to the Generalissimo’s attention and
                    would let me know if the latter had any comments to make or topics he wished to
                    present.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Harriman</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d201-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d201-f1-content">
                <p>The gist of this message was included in telegram No. 11 of July 10 from Grew to
                    Byrnes (file No. 740.00119 Potsdam/7–1045).</p>
